{"id": "pytest_three_failures", "cmd": "cd /work && python -m pytest -v tests", "generator": "pytest_three_failures", "params": {"passed": 2400, "warning_lines": 400}, "gate": "must_pass", "phase": null, "filter_output": true, "checks": {"must_contain": ["$fail_1", "$fail_2", "$fail_3", "$assert_1", "$assert_2", "$assert_3", "$summary", "--- summary ---"], "must_contain_regex": ["^pytest: 3 failed, 2400 passed", "^failed: tests/test_cache.py::test_ttl_expiry"]}, "tags": ["tests", "pytest", "s2", "budget"], "why": "three failures spread through 2,400 PASSED lines with 400 warning lines after the summary; every id, assertion and the summary must survive under budget through priority regions, not position"}
